:'''Firefly:''' That place up ahead is Aideen Park &mdash; everything here is themed around SoulGlad. It's a little crowded, so make sure you stay close to me.
:'''Firefly:''' This is the largest park in Golden Hour &mdash; it represents the soda culture of Penacony. That gigantic soda bottle houses the headquarters of the SoulGlad Enterprise!
:'''Firefly:''' SoulGlad is said to have originated from a sweet medicinal syrup popular during the Prison Era. Invented by a man named Sousa, it was thus called the Sousa Juice. Aideen, an interstellar traveling merchant, saw the potential in the beverage and purchased the formula.
:'''Firefly:''' Aideen then carbonated the beverage and renamed it "SoulGlad." He also pioneered the school of thought known as "Syrupism," in which he promoted the consumption of SoulGlad as a new kind of lifestyle. And just like that, he created a commercial miracle.
:'''Firefly:''' Did you know? One of the ingredients in the original recipe for Sousa Juice, known as Dreamleaf, has gone extinct. That means the only place you can get a taste of Epochal SoulGlad is in Penacony's Dreamscape.
:'''Firefly:''' This is also the only place where one can fully experience the core values of Syrupism...
:She abruptly freezes. In that fleeting moment, you notice a cautious shift in the girl's gaze, piercing directly into your brow, or perhaps somewhere behind you...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What's up?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What are you looking at?
:Firefly returns to her warm and gentle disposition.
:{{tx}}
